### 📌 HMAC Formula & Padding

```
HMAC(K, M) = H [ (K ⊕ opad) || H [ (K ⊕ ipad) || M ] ]

ipad = 0x36 0x36 0x36 ... (repeated B times)
opad = 0x5C 0x5C 0x5C ... (repeated B times)

Block size B = 64 bytes for MD5/SHA-1
              128 bytes for SHA-256
```

---

### 📌 CMAC Subkey Generation Memory Trick

```
Step 1: L = E(K, 0)  [Encrypt all zeros]

Step 2: Generate K1:
   If MSB(L)=0 → K1 = L << 1
   If MSB(L)=1 → K1 = (L<<1) XOR Rb  (Rb=0x87 for AES)

Step 3: Generate K2 (same logic as L→K1):
   If MSB(K1)=0 → K2 = K1 << 1
   If MSB(K1)=1 → K2 = (K1<<1) XOR Rb

Using subkeys:
   Last block complete → use K1
   Last block incomplete → use K2 (pad with 10...0 first)
```

